{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"2a9acfab7a0ae099","name":"card_event_fliegerfuhrer_atlantik","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_fliegerfuhrer_atlantik","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ATLANTIC COMMAND","text":"Move two random Navy cards in your deck to the top.","flavorText":"The Atlantic Command (German: Fliegerführer Atlantik) was a Luftwaffe command formed in 1941 to support German naval operations in the Atlantic during WWII. Its main role was to locate and attack Allied convoys and assist U-boats by spotting targets from the air. The command was based in occupied France and initially operated long-range aircraft such as the Focke-Wulf Fw 200 Condor, later expanding its fleet to include types such as the Heinkel He 177 and Junkers Ju 290. Early on, it helped boost U-boat success, but as Allied air defenses, radar, and escort carriers improved, its effectiveness dropped sharply. The unit suffered heavy losses and struggled to operate as the Allies gained control of the skies and sea lanes. After the Allied invasion of France in 1944 and the loss of key bases, Fliegerführer Atlantik could no longer function effectively and was disbanded later that year.","faction":"Germany","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_fliegerfuhrer_atlantik","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_fliegerfuhrer_atlantik_title","SourceString":"ATLANTIC COMMAND","LocalizedString":"ATLANTIC COMMAND"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_fliegerfuhrer_atlantik_text","SourceString":"Move two random Navy cards in your deck to the top.","LocalizedString":"Move two random Navy cards in your deck to the top."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_fliegerfuhrer_atlantik_history","SourceString":"The Atlantic Command (German: Fliegerführer Atlantik) was a Luftwaffe command formed in 1941 to support German naval operations in the Atlantic during WWII. Its main role was to locate and attack Allied convoys and assist U-boats by spotting targets from the air. The command was based in occupied France and initially operated long-range aircraft such as the Focke-Wulf Fw 200 Condor, later expanding its fleet to include types such as the Heinkel He 177 and Junkers Ju 290. Early on, it helped boost U-boat success, but as Allied air defenses, radar, and escort carriers improved, its effectiveness dropped sharply. The unit suffered heavy losses and struggled to operate as the Allies gained control of the skies and sea lanes. After the Allied invasion of France in 1944 and the loss of key bases, Fliegerführer Atlantik could no longer function effectively and was disbanded later that year.","LocalizedString":"The Atlantic Command (German: Fliegerführer Atlantik) was a Luftwaffe command formed in 1941 to support German naval operations in the Atlantic during WWII. Its main role was to locate and attack Allied convoys and assist U-boats by spotting targets from the air. The command was based in occupied France and initially operated long-range aircraft such as the Focke-Wulf Fw 200 Condor, later expanding its fleet to include types such as the Heinkel He 177 and Junkers Ju 290. Early on, it helped boost U-boat success, but as Allied air defenses, radar, and escort carriers improved, its effectiveness dropped sharply. The unit suffered heavy losses and struggled to operate as the Allies gained control of the skies and sea lanes. After the Allied invasion of France in 1944 and the loss of key bases, Fliegerführer Atlantik could no longer function effectively and was disbanded later that year."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'WolfPack_17'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/WolfPack_17.0"